    <title type="link" role="preferences">Chat</title>
  </info>
  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Chat
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca can announce incoming messages and review recent messages in supported chat
    applications. These applications and settings may refer to conversations as rooms or
    channels.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-chat">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Chat</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak room name</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca includes the conversation name with incoming messages, unless the message came
          from the focused conversation. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak room name last</gui>: Controls whether
          the conversation name is spoken after the message instead of before it. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Announce when your buddies are typing</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca announces changes in typing status when the chat application provides that
          information. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Provide chat room specific message histories</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca keeps separate recent-message histories for each conversation. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak messages from</gui>: Controls which
          incoming chat messages Orca speaks automatically. Choices: All channels when using any
          application, The active channel when using any application, All channels when using
          the application, The active channel when using the application.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>All channels when using any application (default)</gui>: Speaks messages
              from all conversations, even when another application is active.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>The active channel when using any application</gui>: Speaks messages
              from the active conversation, even when another application is active.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>All channels when using the application</gui>: Speaks messages
              from all conversations while the chat application is active.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>The active channel when using the application</gui>: Speaks messages
              from the active conversation while the chat application is active.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-chat">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Chat</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present next chat room message</gui>
          Unbound by default.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present previous chat room message</gui>
          Unbound by default.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle chat room specific message histories</gui>
          Unbound by default.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle room name presentation</gui> Unbound by default.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle typing announcements</gui> Unbound by default.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
